[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Polite Request]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.02]What was the polite request? | 那个客气的请求是什么？
[00:14.64]If you park your car in the wrong place, | 一旦你把汽车停错了地方，
[00:18.11]a traffic policeman will soon find it. | 交通警很快就会发现。
[00:21.68]You will be very lucky if he lets you go without a ticket. | 如果他没给你罚款单就放你走了，算你走运。
[00:26.86]However, this does not always happen. | 然而，情况并不都是这样。
[00:31.48]Traffic police are sometimes very polite. | 交通警有时也很客气。
[00:35.98]During a holiday in Sweden, | 在瑞典度假期间，
[00:38.66]I found this note on my car: | 我在自己的车上发现了这张字条：
[00:42.04]'sir, we welcome you to our city. This is a No Parking area. | “先生，欢迎您光临我们的城市。这是禁停区。
[00:49.85]You will enjoy your stay here if you pay attention to our street signs. This note is only a reminder.' | 如果您对我们街头的标牌加以注意，您在此会过得很愉快的。谨此提请注意。”
[01:00.31]If you receive a request like this, you cannot fail to obey it! | 如果你收到这样的恳求，你不会不遵照执行的！
